# next is pinned to 15.2.3, well behind the fix versions for these CVEs
# (one CRITICAL — CVE-2025-55182, pre-auth RCE via React Server
# Components request deserialization — the rest HIGH: SSRF, DoS),
# because @cloudflare/next-on-pages@1.13.16 (the latest release, as of
# 2026-08-08) cannot build ANY newer 15.x release, including 15.5.2 —
# its own declared peer-dependency ceiling. Verified directly: bumping
# to 15.5.2 or 15.5.15 both produce a real build failure ("The
# following routes were not configured to run with the Edge Runtime:
# /_not-found"), not just a stale peer-range warning.
#
# Accepted as a documented, tracked risk (see ROADMAP.md's Known Risks
# section) rather than blocking every PR indefinitely: this app defines
# no "use server" Server Actions of its own (grepped clean across
# apps/web/app), so the most direct exploitation path isn't reachable
# through app-authored code, though the App Router's own RSC machinery
# is still loaded. Re-evaluate the moment next-on-pages ships a release
# that actually supports a patched Next.js version, or sooner if real
# user traffic/data volume changes the risk calculus.
